{"id": "EUVD-2026-82136", "enisaUuid": "30e6e46a-3043-34c8-bfb9-3710ec036cea", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Preserve unique-field state across nested structs\n\nbtf_find_struct_field() initializes a fresh seen mask for every recursive\ndescent. Unique special fields in different levels of the same aggregate\ntherefore do not see one another. The duplicate fields can reach\nbtf_parse_fields(), where they trigger an invariant WARN_ON_ONCE(). A\ncrafted user BTF can consequently trigger the warning before map creation\nchecks capabilities.\n\nInitialize the seen mask once in btf_find_field() and pass the same pointer\nthrough struct, datasec, and nested-struct walks. This gives the entire field\ntraversal one shared uniqueness state.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:21", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cec97102d4147e18568c93946014c4c8ebf86fcf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28d5f20ed022ade0fb0bfbf50b78fec782083175", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/373a1e9366e711b89bc5e45bd6edf33ef62402cd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f08619f060468076e4acbdc10e0713af20d60e65"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wmq6-chwh-p7qg", "CVE-2026-92515"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2b67db6a-80ac-3747-9fe1-c615c40d57a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64e8ee814819f21beeeda00d4119221443d77992 <cec97102d4147e18568c93946014c4c8ebf86fcf"}, {"id": "377df949-30ee-382e-9b67-eef1ba0297ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "3ce85740-f375-37ef-898f-9bf2764e2d50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "6c78ba28-b40b-3a39-9f29-86e318b29b73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "7b1f45d4-6216-3922-9a3e-52d3ace45aab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64e8ee814819f21beeeda00d4119221443d77992 <f08619f060468076e4acbdc10e0713af20d60e65"}, {"id": "90afe238-6e7b-3c7b-a11f-4984457359e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64e8ee814819f21beeeda00d4119221443d77992 <28d5f20ed022ade0fb0bfbf50b78fec782083175"}, {"id": "a34804a2-ca0f-3491-af2c-86ad0bb5e172", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b8ebcaa2-4dd5-3a74-93cc-8efcec1e6fd1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64e8ee814819f21beeeda00d4119221443d77992 <373a1e9366e711b89bc5e45bd6edf33ef62402cd"}, {"id": "cd65bcba-4903-3c81-b347-3941b2da5b36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e801697a-1036-3709-a502-7ed4897f5601", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "61c424ef-b9eb-3281-82d7-97eb3d70efe0", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}